{"overview":{"Symbol":"MBX","Name":"MBX Biosciences, Inc.","Description":"MBX Biosciences, Inc., a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the discovery and development of precision peptide therapies for the treatment of endocrine and metabolic disorders. Its lead product candidate is Canvuparatide (MBX 2109), a parathyroid hormone peptide prodrug, which is in Phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of chronic hypoparathyroidism. The company is also developing Imapextide (MBX 1416), a long-acting glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor antagonist that is in Phase 2 clinical trial a potential therapy for post-bariatric hypoglycemia, a chronic complication of bariatric surgery. In addition, it is developing MBX 4291, a lead obesity product candidate, which is in investigational new drug-enabling studies for the treatment of obesity and co-morbidities. The company was founded in 2018 and is based in Carmel, Indiana.","CIK":"","Exchange":"NasdaqGS","Currency":"USD","Country":"United States","Sector":"Healthcare","Industry":"Biotechnology","Address":"11711 North Meridian Street, Carmel, IN, 46032, United States","FiscalYearEnd":"","LatestQuarter":"","MarketCapitalization":"1573812480","EBITDA":"-98556000","PERatio":"","PEGRatio":"","BookValue":"9.202","DividendPerShare":"","DividendYield":"","EPS":"-2.17","RevenuePerShareTTM":"","ProfitMargin":"0","OperatingMarginTTM":"0","ReturnOnAssetsTTM":"-0.17676","ReturnOnEquityTTM":"-0.25731","RevenueTTM":"","GrossProfitTTM":"","DilutedEPSTTM":"-2.17","QuarterlyEarningsGrowthYOY":"","QuarterlyRevenueGrowthYOY":"","AnalystTargetPrice":"69.09091","TrailingPE":"","ForwardPE":"-8.402197","PriceToSalesRatioTTM":"","PriceToBookRatio":"3.5932405","EVToRevenue":"","EVToEBITDA":"-10.508","Beta":"","52WeekHigh":"45.85","52WeekLow":"9.43","50DayMovingAverage":"32.1675","200DayMovingAverage":"27.827875","SharesOutstanding":"47597536","DividendDate":"","ExDividendDate":"","DebtToEquity":"0.127"},"daily":{"Meta Data":{"1. Informa